METHOD
Built the real server from the attempt-2 snapshot (`go build ./cmd/server`),
ran it against the tier3 fixture (make_fixture.py — every stored value off
its old step grid: portfolio 2437512.34, healthcare costs/inflations,
phase multiplier 0.93, etc.) with BUDGET2_BACKUP_DIR/IMPORT_DIR under
scratch. Audited the real rendered /whatif page (Playwright + the project's
built tailwind.css/styles.css, not template source or hand-built HTML) with
axe-core 4.13.0 (same copy attempt-1 used:
~/.config/nvm/.../@axe-core/cli/node_modules/axe-core). Forced
`localStorage.theme`/`emulateMedia`/`documentElement.className` to
light/dark explicitly (not relying on prefers-color-scheme), 1440x1000
viewport so the QA panel's `lg:block` isn't hidden. All native <details>
opened; the Quick Adjust drawer opened AND, unlike attempt-1's method, axe
was re-run once per QA TAB (portfolio/rates/phases/healthcare) since each
tab's content is display:none (excluded from the a11y tree) until active —
scanning only the default tab, as attempt-1 did, misses anything gated
behind another tab. Servers killed at end; no :8080 contact; no budget2 MCP
tools; no git state changes; snapshot/scratch-only writes.

AUTOMATED (axe-core, wcag2a/wcag2aa/wcag21aa/wcag22aa, per QA-tab x theme)
