MANUAL — against ACCESSIBILITY.md #4 (labels), #9 (keyboard/focus), #12
(dark parity), #13 (currency sign semantics N/A — no negative values here)
1. Every converted slider (in-card) + its Quick Adjust mirror, across all 4
   QA tabs, both themes (29 range controls with data-quick-adjust-key found
   on the rendered page):
   - Accessible name resolves for every one (`missingLabel: []` in both
     themes) — label[for=] for named controls, aria-label for the phase-
     multiplier QA mirrors (which carry no id, by design, pre-existing).
   - aria-valuetext present and EXACTLY equal to the adjacent visible
     display text at initial render, in BOTH themes, for every WS1-
     converted control (0 mismatches across 29 controls x 2 themes) —
     portfolio ($2,437,512), monthly living expenses, inflation rate,
     investment-return (compound "Fixed 6.3% (overrides allocation)"),
     phase multipliers (100%/93%/80%), and all 4 healthcare fields x 2
     persons (medicare person: monthly cost, post-medicare inflation; ACA
     person: monthly cost, pre-medicare inflation, medicare cost, post-
     medicare inflation) both in-card AND their QA-drawer mirrors.
   - Only 2 controls (+ their QA mirrors) lack aria-valuetext:
     projection-years-slider and tax-deferred-delay-slider. Confirmed via
     `grep` on WS1.2.diff — neither id appears anywhere in the diff; not
     WS1-converted, not in scope, unchanged from master.
   - spending-decline-slider did not render on this fixture (its card is
